"list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float literal `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. Python's `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, which doesn't match the docstring's \"half up\".\n\n**Fix** in `pricing/money.py`: convert the value with `Decimal(repr(x))`, which gives `\"2.675\"` (the shortest text that maps back to the same float). Then round to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and convert back to a float, so callers still get a float.\n\n- Results: `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.665\u21922.67`. `-2.675\u2192-2.68`: for negative values, halves round away from zero.\n- `add_vat` uses this function, so it picks up the fix automatically. `add_vat(10.0)` is still `12.0`.\n\n**Tests:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py` with these cases. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly instead. The new test and the existing `test_split` both pass.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 3, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 209381, "requests_cache_write": 21022, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1918182, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 2238, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial5", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 8, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T04:22:47.085160+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 27.535, "t_checker_s": 0.392, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-bugfix-regress", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "a